@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Medium SysML activity with continuous object flow, rate, control operator.
'   usecase:      Tank-fill loop — streaming flow + «controlOperator» boundaries.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       process-control
' ============================================================================
title Example SysML Activity - Fill Tank (Continuous)

' «continuous» is a SysML stereotype on object/control flow indicating
' a streaming flow (values flow at a rate, not as discrete tokens).
' «controlOperator» is applied to a behavior that enables/disables other
' flows — the SysML "on/off switch" for activities.

|Controller|
:Initialize Setpoint;
:Arm Safety Interlock;

' controlOperator toggles execution of the fill loop on/off.
' Modeled as a stereotyped action comment because PlantUML has no
' first-class control-operator shape.
:<<controlOperator>>
EnableFillLoop;

|Tank|
' continuous object flow: level stream from the tank sensor
:Stream Level Signal
  <<continuous>>
  {rate = 10 Hz};

|Controller|
:Receive Level;
:Compute Fill Rate;

if (Level < Target?) then (yes)
  :Open Inlet Valve;
  ' continuous flow back into the loop — water physically flows
  :Pump Fluid
    <<continuous>>
    {rate = 5 L/s};
else (no)
  :Close Inlet Valve;
endif

:Stream Level Signal
  <<continuous>>
  {rate = 10 Hz};

:<<controlOperator>>
DisableFillLoop;

|Controller|
:Report Status;
stop

note right of EnableFillLoop
  <b>«controlOperator»</b>
  ----
  SysML-specific: an action that
  enables or disables another flow
  rather than producing data.
  Native UML has no equivalent.
end note

note right of Pump Fluid
  <b>«continuous» flow</b>
  ----
  The {rate} annotation is a
  SysML value property describing
  how fast tokens/values stream.
end note

@enduml
